From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QED64 Toolchain <qed64-toolchain@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:12:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] feat: load header snapshots from an in-memory region
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This PR adds CompactedRegion.readMem and lean_wasm_load_snapshot_mem so a host can hand the runtime a snapshot it already streamed into the heap instead of staging the file on a virtual file system first.

The file-based path reads the whole region into a malloc buffer before the relocation walk, so a browser worker that must first write the bytes into MEMFS pays a second multi-GB copy in its JavaScript heap — which is exactly what fails first in memory-constrained renderers (observed: Array buffer allocation failed for a 2.6 GiB whole-Mathlib snapshot). The in-memory reader shares the v2/v3 section parsing and relocation walk with the file reader (finish_region_read) and takes ownership of the caller's malloc buffer as the region's backing store.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
